zlib gz_comp(): when the write that follows Z_STREAM_END fails, set state->reset before the error return, as the
success path does, so the next gzflush(Z_FINISH) or gzclose() writes the finished member instead of nothing.

Defect. gz_comp with flush == Z_FINISH runs deflate() until Z_STREAM_END and then writes the output buffer
(gzwrite.c:111-128 at 99623ef7). When that write() returns -1 (for example EAGAIN on a non-blocking descriptor,
which sets state->again and leaves the file usable), gz_comp returns -1 at gzwrite.c:116-121 and never reaches
`state->reset = 1` (gzwrite.c:144). The deflate stream has already ended, so the next gz_comp(state, Z_FINISH) (a
retried gzflush(file, Z_FINISH), or gzclose_w) gets Z_STREAM_END again from deflate() with no new output and, with
ret == Z_OK at the top of its loop, does not write the pending bytes: it returns 0, the call returns Z_OK, and the
finished member is not written.

Fix. In the write-error branch, when flush == Z_FINISH and ret == Z_STREAM_END, set state->reset = 1 before the
return, as gzwrite.c:143-144 does on success. The pending bytes stay where they are (x.next .. next_out), and the
next gz_comp takes the reset path and writes them, followed by one empty 20-byte gzip member, as 1.4 already does
for any gzflush(Z_FINISH) followed by gzclose (a2b6127); gzread reads the members back as one stream. Nothing
else changes.

Upstream. madler/zlib pull request #1399, "Write the finished gzip stream after a gzflush(Z_FINISH) that stalls."
("Fixes #1398"; open on 2026-11-18), head commit 9e7904dd70bc986cfbea8f6df5937b930dedda96, its only commit (on
99623ef7, gzwrite.c +2/-0). The diff below is that commit's diff; only its index line names the two blobs in full
(the pull request's diff abbreviates them to 32560fe0b..a7a78f170). It applies at aef's pin 99623ef7 with
`patch -p1 --fuzz=0`, after the default patch stack and this target's 0001 and 0002, with no offset or fuzz.

Scope. This patch is applied to the build of targets/zlib-sysfail_fuzzer ONLY, by the pin key LIB_PATCHES
(tools/ossfuzz/recipes.sh aef_lib_patches, on the build's copy of the tree): no other zlib target, and not
ext/zlib-sysfail_fuzzer/src, changes. The default patch stack (patches/github.com/madler/zlib/99623ef7.../)
does not carry it. A release build (AEF_RELEASE=1) applies none of LIB_PATCHES: it is a library-defect fix,
and the public release ships the library without those.

Provenance. ZLIB-8 v5 (2026-11-18): found with the system-call failure driver (a gzflush(Z_FINISH) whose
write-out fails with EAGAIN, then gzclose); Jason's word 2026-11-16 23:33:55Z: patch it.

Author of the fix: Jason Gross and Claude Opus 5.5 (the pull request's commit). Carried unchanged by Claude Opus
5.5 (aef, 2026-11-18).

diff --git a/gzwrite.c b/gzwrite.c
index 32560fe0b026f5573fa30e07646ae902805d83be..a7a78f1702124abc7dece3a49a40182e563121f9 100644
--- a/gzwrite.c
+++ b/gzwrite.c
@@ -116,6 +116,8 @@ local int gz_comp(gz_statep state, int flush) {
                 if (writ < 0) {
                     if (BLOCKED(errno))
                         state->again = 1;
+                    if (flush == Z_FINISH && ret == Z_STREAM_END)
+                        state->reset = 1;
                     gz_error(state, Z_ERRNO, zstrerror());
                     return -1;
                 }
